/-!
# Recovering native structures and arrows from realizations

Chapter 4, §4.5. Constant realization preserves all native Laws and
recovers every structure-preserving arrow over connected nonzero
coefficients. The globally split full subcategory recovers the native
semantic category. The product spectrum gives a disjunction with
different local alternatives, while scalar reading compares a copied
quantity with its value in the coefficient ring.
For tensor realizations, coefficient-natural families of linear
structure-preserving arrows recover exactly the original linear arrows,
including factorizations and value maps on specified submodule domains.
-/
